    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWith 'virtualedit' containing block, Visual-block * / # builds a search pattern with trailing spaces that aren't in the text, so the search fails. getregion() pads blockwise lines with spaces when virtualedit allows the block to extend past the line end, and _visual_search() puts that padding into the pattern.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean +'set virtualedit=block' +'call setline(1, [\"foo bar\", \"x\", \"foo bar\"])'                                                                                                                          \nPress gg0 contral v $*.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe cursor jumps to line 3, as it does with virtualedit= (the default).\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.6\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\ndoesnt have this feature\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narchlinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.49.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nkitty\n\n### Installation\n\narch extra repo",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
