        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "That's just the way `getregion` interacts with virtualedit. Trimming trailing spaces from the pattern would break user expectation when they deliberately go past the end of the line. I figure this should be addressed in `getregion` anyway (if at all). `getregion` could be changed so that if vritualedit is active and the cursor is only one character past the end of the line, the resulting string doesn't include the padding. One reason why this behavior might not be preferable is for the following case (using your example): `gg0<C-V>jl`. WIth a multi-line selection it makes more sense to retain the padding (otherwise, why are you using blockwise visual mode for search at all?).",
