        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hmm, thinking about this some more, isn't this an issue with virtualedit in general? When I used to have it set, I almost never wanted trailing whitespace to be copied with `$y` in visual block mode, but it was useful enough that I kept it set for other cases. Currently, the behavior of `_visual_search` matches the behavior of virtualedit more generally when it is active. Maybe virtualedit could take an additional option which would cause `$` to behave as if it weren't active (i.e. the behavior documented in `v_$`)? I think that would be the best solution.\n\nThoughts?",
